Subject: [REVIEW 04/16] Qualcomm Type-C messaging and USB host behavior

Validate USB4 mode messages and coordinate Type-C/PHY requests. Report which xHCI ports carry a USB3 link tunnelled over USB4 (DWC3 CIO register) and skip U1 on such links, which USB4 does not support (USB4 v2.0 section 9.2.1.1); U2 stays allowed. The September policy that kept tunnelled links out of USB3 link power management and runtime suspend is removed; the U2/U3 exit failures behind it came from GUSB3PIPECTL.DEPOCHANGE, now cleared through the device tree (patch 08). DWC3: the xHCI no longer initializes and powers the PHYs a second time, so an idle combo PHY can runtime-suspend; the PHYs get host mode before a role switch creates the xHCI (the eUSB2 repeater needs its host settings first; without this the Dell reached USB4 about 30 s late at boot). dwc3-qcom prepares the connection wake triggers before a later host starts, because changing a trigger while suspended cleared a pending dock reconnect, keeps the firmware trigger policy for the first host, reports wake-trigger and runtime-PM failures, and no longer dereferences a missing xHCI hcd after a failed probe. Review the scope of these changes on other DWC3 hosts.

Dependencies: Base prerequisites; this patch references no symbols from patch 01. The validated USB4 mode messages are consumed by the Type-C handling in patch 05, which drives the PHY from patch 01. Patches 13 and 14 change the DWC3 files further.

Source attribution: Local Surface integration; provenance/usb4/08-pmic-glink-tbt-payload.diff and 09-pmic-glink-usb4-validation.diff; USB host/hub changes recorded in provenance/derivation.json (Surface candidates through 1.130). Krishna Kurapati posted the same xhci-skip-phy-init approach for dwc3-qcom (patchwork 14814397); this local version is kept until that is merged.

This is a review grouping of preserved source, not a new authorship claim or
an independently build-validated upstream commit. Original attribution remains
in the referenced provenance files. No new Signed-off-by trailers are added.

---
